# Kontakt 8.13 at 100 % (shoot.sh, DPI=96, NODRIVE=1), oracle run 2026-11-25 (gen.py hiding()).
# Each row is an unsized label, a 60 x 18 label and a 16-step table; the rows apply HIDE values in
# order: none; 16 then 0; 0; 1 then 0.
row   hide sequence   label face   table frame and field
0     -               drawn        drawn
1     16, 0           drawn        drawn
2     0               drawn        drawn
3     1, 0            drawn        drawn
# A control hidden whole and shown again draws as one never hidden: the last HIDE value is all
# that counts. KONTRA keeps only the last value, so it draws these rows the same.
